+# EPMCDME-16496: Period-scoped CLI Analytics session listing — Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Make CLI Analytics list and count a session for a given period only when it has real activity (a prompt, an API call, or a tool call) or cost rows in that period, and make the Overview/per-user/per-day counts use the same session universe as the Sessions list — without any new migration, and without any Copilot-specific special-casing.
+
+**Architecture:** The entire session-membership decision for every CLI Analytics query already lives in one function, `PostgresCliAnalyticsReader._sessions_cte` (`sel`), by explicit design (`reader.py:18-21` docstring: "the window is decided once, in `_sessions_cte`"). Today `sel` admits a session when its all-time `session_dims.started_at` falls in `[start, end]` — too broad for an old session resumed-and-closed with no new activity, too narrow for an old-but-still-active session whose `started_at` predates the window. This plan replaces that one predicate with an activity/cost existence check against the day-grain rollup tables that already exist (`turns_daily`, `tool_facts_daily`, `cost_daily`), which are platform-agnostic (Claude Code, Copilot Chat, Copilot CLI all write the same tables), so every downstream query (Sessions list, session detail, Overview, Users, Lines, Efficiency, repositories, heatmap) is corrected by one change at its single source of truth. Fact *values* (turns, cost, tool calls shown per session) stay all-time sums, exactly as before — only *membership* becomes period-scoped; this is a deliberate pre-existing design choice (`reader.py` docstring; "list row numbers are NOT period-clipped") that this task does not revisit. Once membership is fixed, Overview/Users/per-day counts (`get_cost_kpis`, `get_users`, `get_users_daily_activity`) are switched from their own narrower `cost_daily`-only universe onto `sel` (the same costless-inclusive universe the Sessions list already uses via `include_costless=True`), replacing the documented "D1 rule" cost-only restriction. A session with zero activity in *any* period (only `agent.session.start`/`agent.session.env`, e.g. an empty VS Code-restart session) now has no row in `turns_daily`/`tool_facts_daily`/`cost_daily` for any day, so it is excluded from `sel` for every window — satisfying the ticket's "not listed or counted" expectation for empty sessions without any separate dead-session reclassification.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Python 3.12, FastAPI, raw parameterized SQL via asyncpg (no ORM), PostgreSQL 14/17, pytest + pytest-asyncio, live-Postgres test harness (`make test-cli-analytics-live`).
+
+**Spec:** Jira EPMCDME-16496 and its two verification-failure comments (resolved via the Jira lookup in this conversation; no separate spec.md — `sdlc-light` flow); re-derived against current code in `docs/superpowers/tasks/2026-11-03-epmcdme-16496-sessions-without-usage/technical-analysis.md`.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No DB migration or new `session_dims` column — use only the existing day-grain rollup tables (`turns_daily`, `tool_facts_daily`, `cost_daily`).
+- Session/fact-value window membership stays decided in exactly one place, `_sessions_cte` — every other reader method keeps reading `sel`, none gets its own copy of the window predicate.
+- Fact *values* (turns, tool_calls, tokens, cost shown per session) remain all-time sums; this task changes *membership* only, not value scoping.
+- Repository layer owns all SQL; the handler only orchestrates and classifies already-fetched rows (per `.ai-run/guides/data/repository-patterns.md`).
+- `make test-cli-analytics-live` is mandatory and non-skippable for any change under `src/codemie/repository/cli_analytics/postgres/` — must be run and its real output reported before this plan is considered done.
+- No Copilot-specific branching: the new activity predicate and the Overview/Users universe change use the same platform-agnostic tables for Claude Code, Copilot Chat and Copilot CLI sessions alike.
+- Gap (c) — Copilot subagent fragments listed as separate sessions — is explicitly OUT of scope; not reproducible against this repo's current schema/ingest code (confirmed in `technical-analysis.md` §6). No code changes for it; flag back to the reporter if it recurs.
+- These are modifications to functions already core to `reader.py`'s and `cli_analytics_handler.py`'s existing responsibility (the window predicate, the Overview/Users universe) — no new module extraction is required by `.ai-run/guides/standards/code-quality.md`'s "new concern" rule.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- A session whose only in-window event is a tool *error/denied* hook, with no successful tool call, no API call and no prompt in that window — does `tool_facts_daily`/`invocations_hourly` register it, and should it count as "activity"? Pin the decision with a test in Task 1.
+- Window-boundary inclusivity: an activity row whose `day` lands exactly on the UTC date of `start_dt` or `end_dt` (which are truncated to milliseconds, not necessarily midnight) must still be included, matching the existing `test_session_start_boundaries_are_inclusive_at_both_ends` precedent for the old predicate.
+- A session with cost rows but zero `turns_daily`/`tool_facts_daily` rows (e.g. a pure API-replay session with no hook-tracked prompts) must still be admitted via the `cost_daily` arm of the new predicate, not silently dropped.
+- `get_session_page` (SQL-side pagination/sorting, used by `get_sessions` when `sort_by` is a SQL-eligible column) must produce the same total count as the Python-side path once `sel` changes — a session excluded from `sel` must disappear from paged totals too, not just from the full list.
+- Overview `total_sessions` must stay a `count(DISTINCT session_id)` even though a session can now appear via more than one of `turns_daily`/`tool_facts_daily`/`cost_daily` in the same window — no double counting.
