+## 2. Codebase Findings
+
+### Repo state vs. ticket's referenced MR !4659 — IMPORTANT CORRECTION
+
+Both comments reference a BE MR !4659 at successive heads (213371f22, then cccf812a3) that introduces `_IS_LISTED`, an `is_subagent` session_dims column, and a "Filter unlisted sessions in CLI analytics sessions CTE" commit. **None of this exists in the current checkout.**
+
+- Current HEAD is `9991e9326ec990ab858fbc19fc57f98f3719b525` on branch `EPMCDME-16496_sessions-without-usage` (confirmed via `git rev-parse HEAD`).
+- `git log --all --oneline --grep="16496" --grep="16572" --grep="4659" -i` → no hits in any branch/ref for 16496, 16572, or 4659.
+- `git log --all --oneline -S"_IS_LISTED" -- src/codemie` → no results. `git grep -n "_IS_LISTED"` → no results.
+- `git grep -n "is_subagent"` → only an unrelated `is_subagent: bool` flag on CodeMie's own `LangGraphAgent`/`assistant_service.py` multi-agent supervisor — nothing to do with CLI Analytics.
+- The only EPMCDME-16496-family commit present is the precursor `a80c1922c "EPMCDME-16441: Price subagent cost, log gate discards and list cost-less CLI analytics sessions"`.
+
+**Conclusion: this checkout is behind the state the ticket's comments were verified against.** MR !4659 (whatever repo/branch it lives in — possibly not yet merged to this branch, or in a different repo) is the actual locus of the "all-time counters vs. period-scoped" bug from Comment 2. This repo currently has an *earlier* version of the fix (from `a80c1922c`) that already solves the original reported case (sessions without token usage being listed) but has NOT yet picked up the "Filter unlisted sessions" / `is_subagent` work from Comments 1 and 2. The remaining implementation work described below is reasoned from this repo's actual current code, not merely replayed from the ticket comments.
+
+### Existing Implementations
+
+- `src/codemie/repository/cli_analytics/postgres/reader.py` (1331 lines) — sole data-access layer for CLI Analytics dashboards; module docstring (lines 18-21) states the design explicitly: "a session is in the window iff its `started_at` is in `[start, end]` ... the window is decided once, in `_sessions_cte`."
+  - `_sessions_cte` (reader.py:330-372) — the only session-membership predicate in the whole reader. Uses:
+    ```python
+    _STARTED_IN_WINDOW = "started_at BETWEEN $start_dt::timestamptz AND $end_dt::timestamptz"   # line 76
+    ...
+    FROM session_dims d
+    WHERE d.started_at IS NOT NULL AND {_STARTED_IN_WINDOW}                                     # line 370
+    ```
+  - `_scope` (reader.py:386-388) — restricts every fact query to `session_id IN (SELECT session_id FROM sel)` with **no day/ts bound** — once a session is admitted, ALL of its fact rows (cost_daily, lines_daily, turns_daily, etc.) are summed in full regardless of which calendar day they actually fall on.
+  - `get_session_cost_facts` (reader.py:724-766) — `include_costless` param (default `False`) controls `_facts_from` (reader.py:199-209): `False` inner-joins `cost_daily` (requires a cost row); `True` left-joins cost onto every `sel` session so costless sessions appear with NULL cost columns. The Sessions list (handler.py:825) calls this with `include_costless=True`.
+  - `get_session_detail_meta` (reader.py:888-938) — CTE `c` (lines 894-900): `SELECT session_id FROM cost_daily WHERE session_id=$sid UNION SELECT session_id FROM session_dims WHERE session_id=$sid AND started_at IS NOT NULL`. "Session not found" (handler.py:903-904) now fires only when neither a cost_daily row nor a session_dims row with non-null `started_at` exists for that session_id — **the original reported 404-for-costless-session bug appears already fixed** by `a80c1922c`.
+  - `get_cost_kpis` (reader.py:411-425) — Overview's `total_sessions`:
+    ```sql
+    SELECT count(DISTINCT session_id) AS total_sessions, ...
+    FROM cost_daily
+    WHERE true{self._scope(f)}
+    ```
+    This is **still cost_daily-based** — a different, narrower session universe than the Sessions list.
+  - `get_users` (reader.py:478-496) and `get_users_daily_activity` (reader.py:498-507) — both built from `_cost_rows(...)`, also cost_daily-sourced; same narrower universe.
+
+- `src/codemie/service/analytics/handlers/cli_analytics_handler.py` —
+  - `_dead_sessions` (handler.py:481-494):
+    ```python
+    @staticmethod
+    def _dead_sessions(session_money, files_by_session) -> tuple[int, float]:
+        """A session that cost money but touched no file. Returns (count, wasted_usd)."""
+        dead = 0
+        wasted = 0.0
+        for sid, cost in session_money.items():
+            if cost <= 0:
+                continue
+            if _i(files_by_session.get(sid, {}).get("files_changed")) == 0:
+                dead += 1
+                wasted += cost
+        return dead, wasted
+    ```
+    Semantics: "cost > 0 and files_changed == 0" only. Used only in `get_overview` (handler.py:444, 458) and `get_efficiency` (handler.py:1174, 1193-1197) as an aggregate KPI — it does **not** filter the Sessions list, and it explicitly skips `cost <= 0` sessions (`continue`), so a zero-cost, zero-activity session is neither counted as dead nor excluded from `get_sessions`.
+  - D1-rule comments documenting the *deliberate* cost-based Overview universe: handler.py:425-426 `"# D1: the session universe is the priced (cost_daily) one, so every / per-session roll-up below is restricted to those sessions."`; handler.py:607 `"# D1 rule: average duration over priced sessions only (same universe as the overview)"`.
+  - `get_sessions` (handler.py:801-877) calls `get_session_cost_facts(..., include_costless=True)` (handler.py:825) — the costless-inclusive universe, inconsistent with `get_overview`/`get_cost`/`get_users`.
+  - No code anywhere in this file filters empty sessions (only `agent.session.start` + `agent.session.env`) or subagent-fragment sessions out of the listing (grep for "dead"/"subagent"/"empty" found nothing else relevant).
+
+### Architecture and Layers Affected
+
+- **Repository layer**: `src/codemie/repository/cli_analytics/postgres/reader.py` (query construction, session-universe predicate), `rollups.py` (background rollup/aggregation that populates `session_dims`, `cost_daily`, `subagent_invocations`, etc.), `fork_attribution.py` (same-session fork/subagent-dispatch matching), `settings.py` (CLI_ANALYTICS_* config), `ports.py`/`factory.py` (adapter selection).
+- **Service/handler layer**: `src/codemie/service/analytics/handlers/cli_analytics_handler.py` (`get_sessions`, `get_overview`, `get_cost`, `get_users`, `_dead_sessions`, `get_efficiency`) — orchestrates reader calls and applies the "D1 rule" cost-based restriction for Overview/Cost/Users but not for Sessions.
+- **API layer**: `src/codemie/rest_api/routers/cli_analytics.py` — route-level feature-flag gating (`_ensure_enabled`), not implicated in the listing-logic bug itself.
+- **DB/persistence layer**: `src/external/alembic_cli_analytics/versions/` — 3 migration files define `session_dims`, `cost_daily`, `turns_daily`, `tool_facts_daily`, `invocations_hourly`, `subagent_invocations`, etc. No DB layer change is strictly required for the bug fix (see Section 6 / risk indicators) unless subagent-fragment linkage is later substantiated as a real defect.
+
+### Integration Points
+
+- Ingest path (`src/codemie/repository/cli_analytics/postgres/otlp.py`, event-hooks/logs routes) assigns `session_id` directly from each event's own `session.id`/`session_id` attribute at ingest time (otlp.py:683, 752, 842) — no cross-session normalization occurs at ingest.
+- Background rollup jobs (`rollups.py`) populate `session_dims.started_at`/`last_event_at` from the 13 "activity hook events" (`DIMENSION_HOOK_TYPES`, vocabulary.py:81) via `LEAST(sd.started_at, EXCLUDED.started_at)` (rollups.py:1982) — i.e., `started_at` is immutable-earliest-ever, never clipped to any reporting window.
+- Day/hour-grain rollups (`cost_daily.day`, `lines_daily.day`, `turns_daily.day`, `tool_facts_daily.day`, `active_time_daily.day`, `session_files_daily.day`, `invocations_hourly.hour`) already exist and are genuinely period-scoped — these are the natural basis for a period-scoped activity fix, but `_sessions_cte` currently ignores all of them for membership.
+
+### Patterns and Conventions
+
+- Repository boundary convention (per `.ai-run/guides/data/repository-patterns.md`): repositories own data access; services should not bypass repositories. `reader.py` already follows this — all SQL lives there, handler.py orchestrates.
+- Module-size guideline (per `.ai-run/guides/standards/code-quality.md`): soft threshold "avoid adding to a file of about 500 lines or more when the change is not that file's core responsibility — extract first." `reader.py` is **1331 lines**, already well over this threshold; any change to it that isn't core to its existing responsibility (e.g. a new dead-session/subagent-fragment concern) should be extracted into a new module rather than appended, following the precedent of `workspace_script_bridge.py` → `job_bridge.py`/`tool_calling_limits.py`.
+- "Seam Tests for Policy Helpers" convention (`.ai-run/guides/testing/testing-patterns.md`): when a helper/handler encapsulates a listing/dead-session decision, unit-testing the helper alone is insufficient — add a callsite test per branch asserting the boundary value reaches the outer DB query/response object, since a duplicated guard at the callsite can silently go dead.
