+## 3. Documentation Findings
+
+### Guides and Architecture Docs
+
+- `.ai-run/guides/integration/cli-analytics-storage.md` — authoritative storage reference. Key facts directly relevant to this ticket:
+  - **Window semantics documented in the guide itself**: "Sessions list/dashboards include a session iff `session_dims.started_at` is within `[start_dt, end_dt]`. Sessions without `started_at` are excluded entirely" — matches the code finding in Section 2 exactly, confirming the guide is current.
+  - `started_at`/`last_event_at` come ONLY from the 13 activity hook events, never from the six plugin events.
+  - `session_dims` all-time counters: `turns, api_calls, tool_calls, tool_errors, lines_added, lines_removed, files_changed, files_written, files_edited, compaction_count` plus jsonb `commands/skills/agents/tools/models`.
+  - Day/hour-grain "fallback" rollups exist specifically for sessions using OTel-less plugin hooks only: `turns_daily`, `tool_facts_daily`, `invocations_hourly`, `session_files_daily`.
+  - Project gate (`applications.cli_analytics_enabled`, default `false`): a likely independent root cause for "sessions missing from dashboards" if the affected project's ingest is silently discarded (HTTP 200, nothing written) — worth ruling out before assuming the bug is purely in listing logic.
+  - Feature flag `cliAnalytics` (customer-config.yaml, default `enabled: false`) gates the entire route set with 404 if off instance-wide.
+- `.ai-run/guides/integration/cli-analytics-events.md` — six-plugin-event-to-storage mapping; confirms `agent.usage.request` never lands in `hook_events` (only `usage_requests`), and that none of the six plugin events moves `started_at`/`last_event_at` — only the 13 activity hook events do.
+- `.ai-run/guides/quality-gates.md` — `make test-cli-analytics-live` is explicitly called out as mandatory and non-skippable for any change touching `src/codemie/repository/cli_analytics/postgres/` — this bug fix falls squarely in that path.
+- `.ai-run/guides/standards/code-quality.md` — module-size soft-limit guidance (see Patterns above).
+
+### Architectural Decisions
+
+- The cost-based Overview/Cost/Users universe (D1 rule) is a **documented, deliberate** design choice in the current code (handler.py:425-426, 607), not an oversight — any fix to gap (a) must explicitly revisit/remove this documented rule, not just patch around it.
+- `.ai-run/guides/integration/query_pipeline.py:818` carries a related intentional-omission note: `# NOTE: no add_time_range() — intentionally omitted for all-time queries` — documents a parallel all-time/period-scoped distinction elsewhere in the analytics query pipeline; worth checking for consistency/precedent when deciding how to annotate the analogous decision in reader.py.
+- No commit or doc history anywhere in this repo references EPMCDME-16496 or EPMCDME-16572 (`git log --oneline -i --grep="16496" --grep="16572" --all` → empty) — there is no prior architectural-decision trail to draw on beyond the `a80c1922c` precursor commit itself.
