+### Derived Conventions
+
+- SQL lives entirely in `reader.py` as parameterized query-builder functions (no ORM query objects) — any new predicate/column selection follows this same pattern (string-template CTEs assembled via helper constants like `_STARTED_IN_WINDOW`).
+- Dead/classification logic is implemented as small static methods on the handler (`_dead_sessions`) operating on already-fetched dict-shaped rows, not as SQL predicates — a new "empty session" classification should likely follow this same handler-side pattern unless the data is more naturally filtered at the SQL layer (see Section 6).
