+### Feature Flags and Deployment Concerns
+
+- `cliAnalytics` instance-level flag — gates every CLI Analytics route (404 if off) via `_ensure_enabled()` (`src/codemie/rest_api/routers/cli_analytics.py:~142`) and gates background rollup/maintenance jobs (`src/codemie/service/analytics/cli_analytics_jobs.py:89`).
+- `applications.cli_analytics_enabled` — separate per-project DB flag (default `false` for all existing projects post-migration), gates ingestion; a mismatched/missing `X-CodeMie-Project` header or disabled flag causes silent HTTP-200 discard (CLI believes success, deletes spool, never retries) — a plausible independent cause of "missing sessions" symptoms that should be ruled out separately from the listing-logic bug this ticket targets.
+- Background rollup refresh runs on a single pod via advisory locks; a pod on stale code only recomputes families it knows, leaving new columns/tables unpopulated until an explicit backfill (`python -m codemie.repository.cli_analytics.postgres.backfill`) — relevant if any fix here requires backfilling `session_dims`/rollup columns.
